"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"alter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5AlterV","text":"Alter","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV4KindV","text":"Kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Kind-swift.struct"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsObject"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree of the chord being added, altered, or subtracted (1 for the root, 3 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"third, etc.)."}]}],"name":"value"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The chromatic alteration for this degree."}]}],"name":"alter"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this degree is an addition, alteration, or subtraction relative to the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the current chord."}]}],"name":"kind"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if not specified."}]}],"name":"printsObject"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree type is used to add, alter, or subtract individual notes in the chord. The print-object attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used to keep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the degree should be displayed."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Value-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree.Value","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The content of the degree-value type is a number indicating the degree of the chord (1 for the root, 3 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"third, etc). The text attribute specifies how the value of the degree should be displayed. The symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute indicates that a symbol should be used in specifying the degree. If the symbol attribute is present,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value of the text attribute follows the symbol."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)":{"type":"topic","title":"init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLDegree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5ValueV","text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5AlterV","text":"Alter","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV4KindV","text":"Kind","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"printsObject","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/init(value:alter:kind:printsobject:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree.Alter","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree-alter type represents the chromatic alteration for the current degree. If the degree-type value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alter or subtract, the degree-alter value is relative to the degree already in the chord based on its kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. If the degree-type value is add, the degree-alter is relative to a dominant chord (major and perfect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals except for a minor seventh). The plus-minus attribute is used to indicate if plus and minus symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. It is no if not specified."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Kind-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree.Kind","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Kind-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree-type type indicates if this degree is an addition, alteration, or subtraction relative to the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the current chord. The value of the degree-type element affects the interpretation of the value of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degree-alter element. The text attribute specifies how the type of the degree should be displayed."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/kind-swift.struct"}}}